| Annotation              | Definition                                                                                           | Purpose                                                        | Example                                                               |
| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **@NoArgsConstructor**  | Lombok annotation that creates a constructor with no parameters automatically.                       | Avoids writing an empty constructor manually.                  | `Student s = new Student();`                                          |
| **@AllArgsConstructor** | Lombok annotation that creates a constructor with all fields as parameters.                          | Quickly initialize all object values.                          | `Student s = new Student(1,"Teju",22);`                               |
| **@NotBlank**           | Validation annotation that checks a String is not null, empty, or only spaces.                       | Used for mandatory text fields.                                | `"Teju"` ✅, `" "` ❌                                                |
| **@Min(value)**         | Validation annotation that checks a numeric value is greater than or equal to the specified minimum. | Used for age, salary, marks, etc.                              | `@Min(18)` means age must be at least 18.                             |
| **@NotNull**            | Validation annotation that checks a field is not null.                                               | Ensures a value is provided.                                   | `name = null` ❌                                                      |
| **@Validated**          | Spring annotation that activates validation on request data.                                         | Triggers validation annotations like `@NotBlank`, `@Min`, etc. | Used on Controller methods/classes.                                   |
| **@PatchMapping**       | Handles HTTP PATCH requests.                                                                         | Used for partial updates of a resource.                        | Update only a customer's email instead of the entire customer record. |
| **@RequestBody**        | Reads JSON data from the request body and converts it into a Java object.                            | Used when client sends data to the server.                     | POST customer details.                                                |
| **@PathVariable**       | Reads values from the URL path.                                                                      | Used to identify a specific resource.                          | `/students/101` → `101` is the path variable.                         |

