Postman :
Postman is an API testing tool used by developers to send requests to a server and check the responses.
http example : http://localhost:8080/students
--> Instead of creating a webpage to test it, you can use Postman to:
1. Create students
2. View students
3. Update students
4. Delete students
directly from Postman.

Postman Interface : 
1. Request Method Dropdown
GET
POST
PUT
PATCH
DELETE

2. URL Box
http://localhost:8080/students

3. Body Tab --> Used to send JSON data.

4. Headers Tab --> Used to send metadata.
Example:
Content-Type : application/json

5. Response Section
Shows:
{
   "id":101,
   "name":"Teju"
}

HTTP Methods in Postman :
| Method | Operation | Meaning             |
| ------ | --------- | ------------------- |
| GET    | Read      | Fetch data          |
| POST   | Create    | Insert data         |
| PUT    | Update    | Replace entire data |
| PATCH  | Update    | Partial update      |
| DELETE | Delete    | Remove data         |

HTTP Status Codes in Postman :
| Code | Meaning               |
| ---- | --------------------- |
| 200  | OK                    |
| 201  | Created               |
| 204  | No Content            |
| 400  | Bad Request           |
| 401  | Unauthorized          |
| 403  | Forbidden             |
| 404  | Not Found             |
| 500  | Internal Server Error |
